# G3b: a TIMED A/B smoke: V4a only (QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_VALUES): the shard maximum by gather. Read the verify span (projection 0.78 ms saved; the 2-core Reduce is gone). The same three tests as G1 (warmup, coding, concurrent4), the same image, the audits OFF.
# Each arm's verify span, commit phase and live-4 round are read against G3z (the control) in the SAME window: a busy host skews
# every host phase (the speed window's K2 host phases ran 10-20% slower while CI built on the rig): check the load average around the
# run and repeat before believing a gap under about 2 ms.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card verify-glue window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/vglue and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image G0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-vglue-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: set it (in every template of the window) to the tag the driver of the window picks, once
# the image is built from the pushed branch.
# The markers to read (scripts/ci/tp4_vglue.py): '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue engaged site=packed_verify levers=<list> attn_fold=16
# gdn_glue=48 gdn_merge=48 gdn_block_conv=48 shard_values=1' once per captured verify trace (the counts are per layer: 16 attention
# layers, 48 GDN layers; a lever that fell back shows its own *_fallback count instead), '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue engaged site=commit
# lanes=<workers per layer x layers> chips=4' once, and '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue engaged site=sampler shard_values=1' once.
# '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue fell back site=<split|merge|block_conv|attention|sampler> reason=...' is a lever declining (its served path
# ran instead): read every one before trusting a timing, because a fallen-back lever saves nothing. Any '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue audit
# mismatch' line fails the smoke and the gate by itself (c2_smoke_check's 'audit mismatch' rule).
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 5-15 min (the kernels are cached by G1); the three tests 8-15 min: 15 / 30 / 70 min.
# Read: [PACKED-PHASE] (verify: input, trace, sync, readback; commits; early draft; gap) and [PACKED-PUBLISH] per round, medians at 4
# live; the coding decode_tok_s; the concurrent4 per-user decode_tok_s and the [ACCEPT] mean; the lever's own engaged marker and no
# fell-back line for it (the control has no vglue marker at all).
# SOFT: the numbers are the product. The smoke step enforces the stop conditions: an errored or empty stream, garbage text, an audit
# mismatch line.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-vglue-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-vglue-v4a
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4
